  "body": "Chrome doesn't bother with any of this and just reflects as a plain DOMString.\n\nGecko does something like\n\n``` js\nping.split_on_whitespace().map(url_string => {\n  var result = parse(url_string, element);\n  if result.is_error() {\n    return url_string;\n  }\n  return result;\n}).join(\" \");\n```\n",
